Reference only — do NOT git-apply this blindly.

CMake flag placement depends on where your target is created. See README.md,
section "Manual D". The rules are:

  1. add_compile_options() MUST run before the target it should affect is
     created. Appending it at end-of-file does nothing.
  2. If your build globs core/**/*.cpp, speedhack.cpp is picked up
     automatically and you only need the flags.
  3. -ffast-math is safe for the emulator core. Keep it off anything that
     computes cycle timing.
  4. Do NOT add -fno-exceptions or -fno-rtti without testing — the config and
     UI layers use both.

Locate your insertion point with:

    grep -nE 'GLOB|target_sources|add_executable|add_library' CMakeLists.txt

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# [speedhack] Vita performance flags.
+# This block must sit BEFORE the first add_executable / add_library, or the
+# flags will not apply to any target. If your toolchain file already sets
+# some of these, remove the duplicates rather than overriding.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+if(VITA)
+  add_compile_options(
+    -O3
+    -fomit-frame-pointer
+    -ffast-math
+    -fno-math-errno
+    -funroll-loops
+    -ftree-vectorize
+    -mfpu=neon
+    -mfloat-abi=hard
+    -mcpu=cortex-a9
+  )
+
+  # Only needed if the build does NOT glob core/**/*.cpp.
+  # Replace `flycast` with your actual target name.
+  target_sources(flycast PRIVATE core/hw/pvr/speedhack.cpp)
+endif()
